    "name": "Bulgarian Pepper, Hot",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">The Bulgarian Carrot pepper, also known as the Shipka pepper, is an eye-catching heirloom chili variety (</span><i><em class=\"lexical-text-editor--italic\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Capsicum annuum</em></i><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">) highly valued for its striking visual resemblance to a fluorescent orange baby carrot. Originally native to Bulgaria, legend has it that this variety was smuggled from behind the Iron Curtain during the late 1980s before gaining widespread popularity globally.</span></p>",
